WEBVTT

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
Kokoro no mori no naka kimi ni deau koto

00:15.130 --> 00:21.940
I was always dreaming of meeting you

00:16.130 --> 00:22.180
<b>Zettai Shonen</b>

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
Itsumo yume mitetan da

00:21.940 --> 00:26.970
within my heart’s forest.

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
Hikari no silhouette sono saki wo mezashite

00:26.970 --> 00:33.150
The silhouette of light guides the way.

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
Itsuka ai ni furete mitai

00:33.150 --> 00:38.750
One day, I’d like to try and experience love.

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
Kimochi to kotoba niji to mizutamari

00:38.750 --> 00:44.460
My feelings and words can be like rainbows and puddles.

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
Omoiau yasashisa ga michibiku ashita he to

00:44.460 --> 00:51.860
The kindness we share will guide us into tomorrow.

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru kara

00:51.860 --> 00:57.370
With only you here, I can become stronger.

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
Sora takaku negai wo kanadeyou

00:57.370 --> 01:03.680
My wish will be granted in the heights of the sky.

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
Nanika taisetsu ka wo miushinawanu you ni

01:03.680 --> 01:09.050
You won’t lose sight of something precious to you,

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
Kitto motto kagayaku kara

01:09.050 --> 01:18.330
because I’m sure it’ll shine even brighter.

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
Kimi ga iru dake de tsuyoku nareru no sa

01:18.330 --> 01:23.760
With only you here, I can become stronger.

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Ima dekiru koto kara hajimeyou

01:23.760 --> 01:30.140
Let’s start with what we can do right now.

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
Mawarimichi demo ii jibun wo shinjite

01:30.140 --> 01:35.540
I don’t mind if we take a detour, 
as long as you believe in yourself.

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
Kitto motto sono saki he to

01:35.540 --> 01:44.650
By doing that, I’m sure we can go even further.

02:21.020 --> 02:25.020
<b>This is a live feed of the sky
above Yokohama.</b>

02:25.020 --> 02:28.730
<b>We would like the viewers to know
that you are not dreaming.</b>

02:28.730 --> 02:32.600
<b>This is not a movie set,
special effects, or an illusion.</b>

02:32.600 --> 02:38.300
<b>This is the true form of the mysterious Colossus
that has appeared above Yokohama, Japan.</b>

02:47.540 --> 02:54.540
<b>The Dark Lights that Bring Fortune</b>

03:06.230 --> 03:09.500
<b>The diameter of the Colossus is
approximately 5 km in length.</b>

03:09.500 --> 03:15.270
<b>A Colossus Appears in Yokohama!</b>

03:10.170 --> 03:12.970
<b>We’ve confirmed that its eye, or something spherical in shape...</b>

03:12.970 --> 03:15.270
<b>...appears at the center of the being.</b>

03:16.370 --> 03:18.540
<b>However, we have yet to determine...</b>

03:18.540 --> 03:22.010
<b>...whether it’s actually a machine or something else entirely.</b>

03:22.010 --> 03:27.990
<b>Special Live Emergency Broadcast</b>

03:22.840 --> 03:27.990
<b>Investigation!</b>

03:23.580 --> 03:27.990
<b><i>Chasing the Colossus</i></b>

03:27.990 --> 03:33.220
<b>I’d like to open this program by telling all our
viewers out there in their living rooms...</b>

03:33.230 --> 03:37.190
<b>...that the images you just saw on
the news are completely real.</b>

03:39.230 --> 03:42.600
<b>Good day. I am Waga Itsuo.</b>

03:41.370 --> 03:55.280
<b><i>Chasing the Colossus</i></b>

03:41.370 --> 03:55.280
<b>Investigation!</b>

03:42.600 --> 03:46.340
<b>Man-made images are constantly moving
closer and closer to reality.</b>

03:46.340 --> 03:49.170
<b>All around the planet...</b>

03:49.170 --> 03:52.980
<b>...video games appear seemingly
realistic and full CG movies are being made...</b>

03:52.980 --> 03:55.280
<b>...as if reality is becoming the illusion.</b>

03:55.280 --> 04:00.290
<b>Anchor</b>

03:55.280 --> 04:00.290
<b>Waga Itsuo</b>

03:55.280 --> 04:10.500
<b>Investigation!
Yokohama</b>

03:55.280 --> 04:10.500
<b>Chasing the
Colossus</b>

03:55.280 --> 04:00.280
<b>We are living in an age where the line between
the real and the virtual has blurred.</b>

04:01.390 --> 04:07.160
<b>However, the Colossus that has appeared in the
skies above Yokohama does indeed exist.</b>

04:07.160 --> 04:10.490
<b>Several million people
have witnessed it.</b>

04:14.470 --> 04:19.600
<b>It certainly is colossal, but has anyone ever
seen a flying object like this before?</b>

04:19.600 --> 04:20.910
<b>Yes.</b>

04:20.910 --> 04:23.110
<b>In Japan, we’ve had reports
of large UFOs...</b>

04:23.110 --> 04:27.450
<b>...extending up to 1 km in length, dwarfing jumbo jets.</b>

04:27.450 --> 04:34.220
<b>This gigantic UFO flew over 10,000 feet high
and was witnessed by a number of pilots.</b>

04:34.220 --> 04:38.460
<b>The interesting part was that it didn’t
show on any of their control radars.</b>

04:38.460 --> 04:42.430
<b>This Yokohama Colossus isn’t appearing
on any radars, either.</b>

04:42.990 --> 04:48.370
<b>Which is why I don’t think it’s too far-fetched
to say that this is the same type of UFO.</b>

04:49.170 --> 04:52.470
<b>What do you think it is?</b>

04:52.470 --> 04:55.610
<b>They were saying it’s a UFO or something on TV.</b>

04:55.610 --> 04:58.280
<b>My husband can’t get home because of it.</b>

04:58.280 --> 05:02.480
<b>The trains have been stopped, and it seems like
all the roads have been closed to traffic, as well.</b>

05:02.480 --> 05:05.080
<b>My... have you gotten in touch with him?</b>

05:05.080 --> 05:09.190
<b>My cell phone connects...
but then almost instantly cuts off.</b>

05:09.190 --> 05:12.060
<b>Really... for something strange like
this to suddenly appear here...</b>

05:12.060 --> 05:15.460
<b>Someone really needs to do something about it.</b>

05:15.460 --> 05:21.900
<b>Task
Force
HQ</b>

05:15.890 --> 05:20.430
<b>We also have many eyewitness reports from
astronauts saying they’ve seen UFOs.</b>

05:20.430 --> 05:23.930
<b>You see, the Apollo Project was also
a UFO investigation project.</b>

05:24.370 --> 05:27.370
<b>If we were to assume that
it’s here to invade...</b>

05:27.370 --> 05:30.680
<b>...exactly why would the aliens come after the Earth?</b>

05:30.680 --> 05:39.390
<b>Tatewaki
Ryuusuke</b>

05:30.680 --> 05:39.390
<b>Alien researcher</b>

05:30.680 --> 05:37.310
<b>If these aliens are an aggressive species that
tends to invade planets like our own...</b>

05:37.320 --> 05:39.380
<b>...then it’s clear that their goal
would be our resources.</b>

05:39.380 --> 05:41.620
<b>You’re saying that their goal is the same as ours?</b>

05:41.620 --> 05:43.290
<b>It shouldn’t be any different.</b>

05:43.290 --> 05:47.360
<b>People, seen through the eyes of an
alien species, are lowlier than cows.</b>

05:47.360 --> 05:51.000
<b>If we assume that the aliens came for friendly reasons...</b>

05:51.000 --> 05:54.330
<b>...how do you think we should
deal with them?</b>

05:54.330 --> 05:58.440
<b>That may indeed be the case, because
due to a great disaster or something...</b>

05:55.830 --> 06:02.040
<b>Investigation!
Yokohama</b>

05:55.830 --> 06:02.040
<b>Chasing the
Colossus</b>

05:58.440 --> 06:02.040
<b>...their planet may have been destroyed
and they decided to migrate to Earth.</b>

06:02.610 --> 06:05.840
<b>In other words, you’re trying to say that this
gigantic UFO is actually a refugee ship...</b>

06:05.840 --> 06:08.550
<b>...and they’re coming here because of Japanese
governmental laws concerning such people...</b>

06:08.550 --> 06:11.020
<b>...so they believe the government will have
to do something to accommodate them.</b>

06:11.020 --> 06:13.050
<b>That’s exactly what I’m saying.</b>

06:13.050 --> 06:15.050
<b>A UFO, they say?</b>

06:15.050 --> 06:18.690
<b>What kind of countermeasures do they think
we have against something that huge?</b>

06:24.160 --> 06:27.770
<b>Why don’t we start by summarizing
what we’ve established so far?</b>

06:27.770 --> 06:29.270
<b>I agree.</b>

06:29.270 --> 06:35.610
<b>Instead of the Colossus, though, I’d like to
consider the effects its appearance has caused.</b>

06:35.610 --> 06:39.080
<b>That should cause the crux of this
affair to float to the surface.</b>

06:39.810 --> 06:42.010
<b>Since the initial appearance of
the Colossus in Yokohama...</b>

06:42.010 --> 06:46.950
<b>...we’ve had endless reports of trouble with
computers and devices using RF signals.</b>

06:46.950 --> 06:49.570
<b>Many systems with infrared networks...</b>

06:49.570 --> 06:52.560
<b>...such as the Train Automatic Drive System, ETC, ATMs at banks...</b>

06:52.560 --> 06:58.530
<b>...all the way to convenience store registers,
have gone into chaos and stopped working.</b>

06:58.530 --> 07:00.340
<b>More than likely...</b>

07:00.340 --> 07:03.870
<b>...the Colossus is releasing very powerful electromagnetic waves throughout the area.</b>

07:03.870 --> 07:08.210
<b>Yes... and there have apparently been multiple
occurrences of vehicular failures and accidents.</b>

07:08.210 --> 07:11.140
<b>It’s because all these new vehicles nowadays
have computers installed in them.</b>

07:11.140 --> 07:14.450
<b>I really can’t see this Colossus in a favorable light.</b>

07:14.450 --> 07:15.600
<b>At the very least...</b>

07:15.600 --> 07:18.850
<b>...it doesn’t seem like it’s considering
how it’s bothering the citizens who live here.</b>

