<b>Yes...</b>

09:51.970 --> 09:53.300
<b>Turn off the stove, will you?</b>

09:55.810 --> 10:01.780
<b>Everyone, this Colossus is the
savior we’ve been waiting for!</b>

10:01.780 --> 10:07.120
<b>The savior has appeared to save this
defiled Earth and guide the people!</b>

10:07.120 --> 10:17.330
<b>m 462 142.75 l 475.25 136.75 502.75 132 507.625 136.75 540 355.25 494.375 361.25</b>

10:07.120 --> 10:17.330
<b>God is Watching</b>

10:07.120 --> 10:17.330
<b>The Ship of God has come now</b>

10:07.850 --> 10:13.660
<b>Now throw away your desires, join hands,
and let us depart to the promised land!</b>

10:13.660 --> 10:18.100
<b>Only the chosen will be able to walk
into the future that awaits us!</b>

11:21.160 --> 11:23.730
<b>Power outages all through Yokohama...</b>

11:25.300 --> 11:26.660
<b>Gas has also been cut off...</b>

11:28.170 --> 11:32.900
<b>An evacuation alert...
Do we also have to escape from this?</b>

11:34.240 --> 11:36.610
<b>Rieko, where are you going?</b>

11:36.610 --> 11:39.740
<b>Hana-san’s. I’m worried about her,
so I’m gonna go see how she’s doing.</b>

11:41.650 --> 11:44.320
<b>This might be the end for our fish.</b>

11:52.260 --> 11:53.490
<b>Grammy!</b>

11:54.430 --> 11:56.690
<b>Huh? If I remember correctly,
today’s your day off.</b>

11:56.700 --> 11:59.200
<b>You’re keeping the store open?!</b>

11:59.200 --> 12:01.600
<b>An evacuation alert
has been given, you know.</b>

12:01.600 --> 12:02.800
<b>I know.</b>

12:02.800 --> 12:04.470
<b>You have to hurry and evacuate.</b>

12:04.470 --> 12:05.770
<b>Why?</b>

12:05.770 --> 12:07.270
<b>Because...</b>

12:07.270 --> 12:09.510
<b>As I thought, you’re open.</b>

12:09.510 --> 12:11.210
<b>Oh? Welcome.</b>

12:11.210 --> 12:14.110
<b>I didn’t think you’d close your restaurant, Hana-san.</b>

12:14.110 --> 12:16.880
<b>That smells pretty good.
It’s pike, right?</b>

12:16.880 --> 12:19.120
<b>In that case, I’ll have the pike set meal.</b>

12:19.120 --> 12:21.550
<b>We serve Western-style food here.</b>

12:21.550 --> 12:24.260
<b>This is my dinner.</b>

12:24.260 --> 12:26.260
<b>Oh, is that so?</b>

12:26.260 --> 12:27.590
<b>But I guess it’s all right.</b>

12:27.590 --> 12:31.860
<b>The freezer stopped working,
so it’s better than having it go bad.</b>

12:34.030 --> 12:36.270
<b>There we go!
The rice is boiled.</b>

12:37.970 --> 12:40.500
<b>Umm... aren’t you going to evacuate?</b>

12:42.010 --> 12:43.770
<b>Hey, Hana-san.</b>

12:44.740 --> 12:47.240
<b>Wel... come...</b>

12:51.620 --> 12:52.680
<b>I’m back...</b>

12:54.120 --> 12:57.150
<b>Thank goodness.
I still have electricity here.</b>

13:02.560 --> 13:07.260
<b>After walking home from work,
my legs feel like they’re gonna fall off.</b>

13:08.900 --> 13:10.630
<b>I’m a little unhappy here...</b>

13:10.640 --> 13:15.270
<b>Why are you trying to distort the truth
by saying it’s a UFO or aliens?</b>

13:12.140 --> 13:19.640
<b>Asatsumi
Todayuki</b>

13:12.140 --> 13:19.640
<b>Plasma
Researcher</b>

13:15.270 --> 13:16.770
<b>Then what do you suppose it is?</b>

13:18.380 --> 13:20.440
<b>Nothing more than plasma, of course.</b>

13:20.450 --> 13:25.950
<b>Over 99% of the material that space
is composed of is in a plasma state.</b>

13:25.950 --> 13:32.060
<b>And the Colossus that appeared in the skies
of Yokohama is a perfect example.</b>

13:32.060 --> 13:33.000
<b>There’s no doubt about it.</b>

13:41.170 --> 13:43.240
<b>So it finally reached me...</b>

13:44.070 --> 13:45.570
<b>Sorry to keep you waiting.</b>

13:49.340 --> 13:51.180
<b>Please take your time.</b>

13:51.180 --> 13:52.240
<b>Good grief.</b>

13:53.580 --> 13:55.910
<b>We’re only busy at times like these, huh?</b>

13:55.910 --> 13:59.380
<b>But did you see the huge thing, Gen-san?</b>

13:59.380 --> 14:03.150
<b>Yeah... it sure was pretty big, wasn’t it?</b>

14:03.160 --> 14:06.260
<b>The elderly sure have guts...</b>

14:06.260 --> 14:09.630
<b>When you age,
you stop getting panicky.</b>

14:09.630 --> 14:11.030
<b>Why?</b>

14:11.030 --> 14:15.330
<b>Perhaps... because they’re already aware of
what they can do against whatever it is.</b>

14:16.370 --> 14:19.370
<b>Whether they jump the gun or run away in cowardice...</b>

14:19.370 --> 14:21.810
<b>...nothing good usually comes of it.</b>

14:21.810 --> 14:22.910
<b>Really?</b>

14:23.540 --> 14:27.510
<b>No matter how stormy your
days are, time will still pass.</b>

14:28.080 --> 14:30.680
<b>It’s because they messed up in times
like this when they were younger.</b>

14:32.480 --> 14:36.850
<b>Settle down, will you?
This isn’t a bar!</b>

14:36.860 --> 14:41.130
<b>Rieko-chan, could you let this
beer chill outside for a little?</b>

14:41.130 --> 14:42.060
<b>Sure.</b>

14:52.340 --> 14:53.570
<b>This letter is...</b>

15:02.350 --> 15:07.120
<b>The majority of things we call
UFOs or ghosts are “critters.”</b>

15:07.120 --> 15:11.560
<b>When I say “critter,” as its definition suggests, it’s a “living creature.”</b>

15:11.560 --> 15:15.260
<b>Then you’re saying that the Colossus is
a living creature with a will of its own?</b>

15:15.260 --> 15:18.830
<b>I don’t believe in the existence of aliens.</b>

15:18.830 --> 15:24.310
<b>UMA Researcher</b>

15:18.830 --> 15:24.300
<b>But I’m confident that spatially-living
creatures exist and are active in a plasma state.</b>

15:24.940 --> 15:32.440
<b>I hear that in the ancient ruins of Africa,
there are murals that look like that swirly thing.</b>

15:32.440 --> 15:35.550
<b>But if it was just a mural,
then it could’ve been anything.</b>

15:35.550 --> 15:39.250
<b>But anyway, don’t you think that thing’s such a pain?</b>

15:39.250 --> 15:41.450
<b>Just what is the Self-Defense Force doing?</b>

15:41.450 --> 15:43.850
<b>Hurry and blow it up already!</b>

15:43.860 --> 15:48.890
<b>No way. If they shot that thing down, it’d crash
on us and we’d be flattened into pancakes!</b>

15:48.890 --> 15:50.230
<b>Ah, I guess you’re right!</b>

15:54.400 --> 15:57.600
<b>This chain letter... is it the one everyone’s
been talking about?</b>

15:57.600 --> 15:59.570
<b>Huh? You got one, too?</b>

15:59.570 --> 16:01.470
<b>“The dark lights...”</b>

16:03.240 --> 16:04.940
<b>“...bring fortune.”</b>

16:08.150 --> 16:11.450
<b>Could it be that we’re really lucky?!</b>

16:14.920 --> 16:21.860
<b>Now then, experts of various fields have postulated the true identity of this Colossus.</b>

16:21.860 --> 16:39.110
<b>Investigation!
Yokohama</b>

16:21.860 --> 16:39.110
<b>Chasing the
Colossus</b>

16:21.860 --> 16:23.660
<b>We’ve heard that it’s a UFO, the American army...</b>

16:23.660 --> 16:28.530
<b>...plasma, a “critter,” and many other things, but–</b>

16:27.030 --> 16:28.530
<b>You’re all completely wrong.</b>

16:28.530 --> 16:29.770
<b>You’re wasting your time.</b>

16:30.970 --> 16:33.140
<b>Everyone’s mistaken.</b>

16:33.140 --> 16:39.110
<b>Sukawara Akira</b>

16:33.140 --> 16:39.110
<b>Freelance Journalist</b>

16:33.140 --> 16:36.470
<b>Umm... what do you mean, Sugawara-san?</b>

16:36.480 --> 16:39.110
<b>That’s Su-ka-wa-ra.
Be careful not to misread it.</b>

16:39.610 --> 16:43.310
<b>Ah, excuse me.
So, what did you mean by that?</b>

16:43.320 --> 16:46.080
<b>This isn’t the first time something
like this has happened.</b>

16:47.090 --> 16:51.620
<b>Two summers ago, in a small town near
the isthmus of the Izu Peninsula...</b>

16:51.620 --> 16:56.060
<b>...a phenomenon occurred that would be
a harbinger to what’s happening here.</b>

17:00.630 --> 17:03.270
<b>And what phenomenon was that?</b>

17:03.270 --> 17:04.470
<b>The details are in this book.</b>

17:04.470 --> 17:09.440
<b>“The Summer of the Fairies, ~Material Fairies~,” if you’d please read it.</b>

17:09.940 --> 17:13.340
<b>Ah... I’m sorry,
but what is a “material fairy”?</b>

17:13.350 --> 17:15.580
<b>Do you need that explained right now?</b>

17:15.580 --> 17:17.450
<b>Yes... if you could, please.</b>

17:17.450 --> 17:18.480
<b>Very well.</b>

17:19.180 --> 17:22.570
<b>There have been rumors this winter of “dark lights that bring fortune...”</b>

17:22.570 --> 17:25.990
<b>...spread by middle schoolers.</b>

17:25.990 --> 17:27.220
<b>You didn’t know about that, did you?</b>

17:28.230 --> 17:32.700
<b>This. This cold-colored light is one of
those “dark lights that bring fortune.”</b>

17:32.700 --> 17:34.800
<b>And that’s a material fairy?</b>

17:35.270 --> 17:37.400
<b>No. Don’t jump to conclusions.</b>

17:37.300 --> 17:42.780
<b>Sukawara
Akira</b>

17:37.300 --> 17:42.780
<b>Freelance
Journalist</b>

17:37.400 --> 17:42.770
<b>There’s another type, warm in color, which the
rumors say brings you misfortune if you see it.</b>

17:43.340 --> 17:44.980
<b>Warm-colored lights?</b>

17:44.980 --> 17:49.350
<b>That’s right. The warm-colored
lights are the material fairies.</b>

17:49.350 --> 17:52.310
<b>The cold-colored lights are material evils...</b>

17:52.310 --> 17:54.650
<b>That’s what I’m provisionally calling them, at least.</b>

17:54.650 --> 17:56.220
<b>That’s what I was talking about.</b>

17:56.220 --> 17:58.520
<b>Ah... then don’t you have their names backwards?</b>

17:58.520 --> 18:00.390
<b>No.</b>

18:00.390 --> 18:06.230
<b>The pale blue lights that are said to bring
fortune are in reality the evil ones.</b>

18:06.830 --> 18:10.370
<b>The children have simply misread their true nature.</b>

18:10.370 --> 18:12.440
<b>How can you say that?</b>

18:12.440 --> 18:18.880
<b>Like I was saying, I encountered those
material fairies myself two years ago.</b>

18:18.880 --> 18:20.250
<b>I had to digress in the book...</b>

18:20.250 --> 18:22.510
<b>...but this isn’t something
that has happened for the first time.</b>

18:23.220 --> 18:24.450
<b>If I can continue...</b>

18:24.450 --> 18:28.250
<b>...this is nothing more than a single
manifestation in a continuing set of affairs...</b>

18:28.250 --> 18:31.490
<b>...that’s been repeating itself since ancient times.</b>

18:31.920 --> 18:34.460
<b>That’s what I believe.</b>

