<b>Tsukumogami</b>

18:39.870 --> 18:42.500
<b>You’re talking about... spirits?</b>

18:42.500 --> 18:45.300
<b>The ones that are said to have taken
on the form of very old items.</b>

18:45.300 --> 18:49.210
<b>Yes. In the Muromachi era, they were described in a fairy tale as the following...</b>

18:50.240 --> 18:54.310
<b>“Once its receptacle has aged a century,
and transforms to the spiritual...”</b>

18:54.310 --> 19:00.280
<b>“...it deceives the human heart. These beings
are known and named the Tsukumogami.”</b>

19:00.290 --> 19:01.690
<b>Yes...</b>

19:01.690 --> 19:05.420
<b>Since time immemorial, Japan has
had a myriad of different spirits.</b>

19:05.420 --> 19:08.360
<b>They obviously exist in the mountains
and rivers in nature...</b>

19:08.360 --> 19:12.900
<b>...but spirits even reside in stoves and toilets,
which are items people have created.</b>

19:12.900 --> 19:15.970
<b>They say if you treat containers or furniture poorly...</b>

19:15.970 --> 19:18.100
<b>...a spirit will decide to live
in it in the future.</b>

19:18.100 --> 19:20.220
<b>And those items which have become Tsukumogami spirits...</b>

19:20.220 --> 19:22.910
<b>...will march in the streets of the capital.</b>

19:22.910 --> 19:29.210
<b>In lutes and panpipes, shoes, fans,
pots, kettles, and trivets...</b>

19:29.210 --> 19:32.120
<b>...the demons residing in them make up what
we call the “Parade of 100 Demons.”</b>

19:32.120 --> 19:35.390
<b>You’re aware of this parade, correct?</b>

19:35.390 --> 19:37.080
<b>Yes...</b>

19:37.790 --> 19:41.290
<b>According to some old books,
when this event occurred...</b>

19:41.290 --> 19:44.560
<b>...the shocked Emperor summoned many
respectable monks and priests to pray.</b>

19:45.300 --> 19:49.730
<b>And once they did, many bright lights
appeared above the palace.</b>

19:49.730 --> 19:50.530
<b>Lights...</b>

19:51.440 --> 19:55.970
<b>The people of that time thought of those
lights as the servants of Acalanatha.</b>

19:55.970 --> 19:58.510
<b>And the Tsukumogami that were
exterminated repented...</b>

19:58.510 --> 20:03.510
<b>...and eventually accepted the teachings
of Buddha and passed on to Heaven.</b>

20:03.520 --> 20:07.750
<b>In other words, you’re saying that the
Tsukumogami were material evils...</b>

20:07.750 --> 20:12.090
<b>...and the lights that were assumed to be the
servants of Acalanatha were material fairies.</b>

20:12.090 --> 20:13.090
<b>That’s my main point!</b>

20:13.090 --> 20:14.790
<b>Yes...</b>

20:14.790 --> 20:17.060
<b>I’d like you to really think about this for a minute.</b>

20:18.430 --> 20:21.620
<b>These beings that have come from the framework of our world...</b>

20:21.620 --> 20:24.200
<b>...have existed since ancient times.</b>

20:24.200 --> 20:27.400
<b>When mankind didn’t have the capacity to describe these things...</b>

20:27.400 --> 20:30.340
<b>...they were labeled natural phenomena...</b>

20:30.840 --> 20:34.150
<b>...but there’s no way that can explain everything.</b>

20:34.150 --> 20:37.310
<b>Phenomena that would seem out of this world
had already been occurring in those times.</b>

20:37.320 --> 20:45.790
<b>It’s true that the first UFO was said to have
been witnessed in 1947 by Kenneth Arnold...</b>

20:45.790 --> 20:49.190
<b>...but if we look even further back, it’s not a
stretch to say that tons of records exist...</b>

20:49.190 --> 20:53.200
<b>...that could be considered UFO appearances
in ancient literature.</b>

20:53.200 --> 20:54.470
<b>Thank you.</b>

20:54.470 --> 20:57.540
<b>We may have called it different
things though the ages...</b>

20:57.540 --> 21:01.340
<b>...but the facts all point to the same
phenomenon existing. Don’t you agree?</b>

21:03.610 --> 21:09.150
<b>Which is why I don’t think it’s hard to believe
that all the spirits, monsters, fairy tales...</b>

21:09.150 --> 21:11.880
<b>...and the legends and myths that surround
them that are scattered across the world...</b>

21:11.880 --> 21:22.360
<b>...are all different forms of the opposition between
material evils and material fairies. Right?</b>

21:22.360 --> 21:25.830
<b>Then this UFO is..</b>

21:25.830 --> 21:32.340
<b>I think that Colossus in the sky
is just a huge material evil...</b>

21:32.840 --> 21:38.310
<b>...or maybe a huge material fairy,
which would be its opposite.</b>

21:38.840 --> 21:43.510
<b>So you think that the Colossus,
which you call a huge material evil...</b>

21:43.520 --> 21:47.600
<b>...is just one huge Tsukumogami that was living within all the waste...</b>

21:47.600 --> 21:49.950
<b>...expended by modern-day factories?</b>

21:49.960 --> 21:53.090
<b>I think the balance between the two types crumbled
 somewhere along the line, so that was created.</b>

21:53.090 --> 22:00.230
<b>Maybe there was a low number of material fairies
that were supposed to purify the material evils.</b>

22:00.230 --> 22:05.240
<b>So that basically means... er, what exactly
are we supposed to do now, then?</b>

22:05.240 --> 22:07.440
<b>If the UFO is to come at us...</b>

22:08.240 --> 22:10.610
<b>I’m a journalist.</b>

22:10.610 --> 22:14.310
<b>I witness events, and I’m nothing more than
someone who relays them to the people.</b>

22:14.310 --> 22:16.610
<b>I don’t know how to cope with them.</b>

22:16.620 --> 22:17.580
<b>No way...</b>

22:17.580 --> 22:21.550
<b>But... at the very least, I will...</b>

22:30.360 --> 22:34.770
<b>...think and act about it.</b>

22:38.170 --> 22:41.670
<b>I feel that that’s something people
should never stop doing.</b>

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
Daremo shiranai kotoba de kimi he to

22:52.250 --> 22:59.820
On that nostalgic hill, I sang out to you

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
Utaikaketa natsukashii oka de

22:59.820 --> 23:06.530
words that no one else knew.

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
Tomare soyokaze kawaranu omoide

23:09.530 --> 23:17.030
The dying breeze and my unchanged memories

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
Sotto misete ano koro no boku wa

23:17.030 --> 23:23.710
gently reveal to me what I was like back then.

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Aa yume wo aishite hitori ni natta

23:23.710 --> 23:31.150
Ah, I thought that being alone

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
Sore de ii to omotta

23:31.150 --> 23:35.950
and cherishing my dream would be fine.

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
Haruka na sora ni wa ima mo kimi ga iru darou

23:35.950 --> 23:44.630
I wonder if you’re still there right now in the distant sky?

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Yasashiku ikiru yo afureru namida koraeta

23:44.630 --> 23:53.230
Now I lead a simple life, having suppressed my overflowing tears.

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
Mirai no melody ga shizuka ni yureru kisetsu

23:53.230 --> 24:02.010
The melody of the future is in the quietly stirring seasons.

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
Aitai na itsu no hi ka... mattete

24:02.010 --> 24:10.720
I want to see you again, and I’m waiting for that day.

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
Aitai ne boku wa mada humming boy

24:10.720 --> 24:19.260
I want to see you again, but I’m still a humming boy.

